  "reconstructibility": 1,
  "reason": "The records establish several important ingredients: lamellar-interface stress localization and cracking in eutectic HEAs, the stress-relieving role of distributed microcracking, benefits of coherent internal boundaries, hierarchical architectures, FCC deformation by stacking faults and twins, and load transfer or transformation in hard B2-containing Al-Co-Cr-Fe-Ni alloys. They also provide related pressure/temperature processing precedents through HPT, SPS, and hot-working plus annealing. However, none describes hexahedron-anvil HPHT treatment of a homogenized Al0.7CoCrFeNi eutectic alloy or shows that it converts incoherent FCC/B2 lamellae into a coherent hierarchical pattern enabling preferential FCC-to-B2 dislocation transfer. Thus the literature points toward the desired microstructure and mechanism, but selecting the specific HPHT intervention would require a substantial new idea."
